"axJ" = (
/obj/structure/bed/chair/office/light{
	pixel_y = -4
	},
/obj/item/remains/mummy2,
/obj/item/device/radio/headset{
	icon_state = "bs_bowman_headset"
	},
/obj/structure/snowfall{
	name = "dust";
	light_color = "#8B0000";
	light_range = 1;
	desc = "Thick dust fills the air"
	},
/obj/item/implant/uplink,
/obj/item/paper{
	info = "This is it.The entrance caved in hours ago. The dust is still settling, but it doesn’t matter now. Every system’s breaking down—power’s flickering out, comms are dead, and the reactor's barely holding. We thought we could fix it, we hoped we could. But it's too late. It’s all collapsing, and there’s no escape.It’s… spreading. That thing, whatever’s left of it, it’s seeping through the vents, crawling through the walls. It’s twisting everything—eating everything. You can smell it now. The air’s thick with rot, with something that shouldn’t exist. We’re trapped. And no one’s coming. Not the team, not the higher-ups. Sakaba Corp... they’ve left us here to die. They know what’s happening, and they’re not lifting a finger.We did this. We let it all happen. Every time we turned a blind eye, every decision we made to push forward when we should’ve stopped… this is what we deserve. Alpha wasn’t our future—it was a grave from the start, we just didn’t see it. Now it’s taking us with it.I’ve seen them. The others—what's left of them. Warped, twisted into those things, shambling around in the dark, hunting anything that moves. It’s them, Marcus, they’re still in there, in some sick, grotesque way. I can’t even look anymore. We brought this on ourselves, and now it's justice. A slow, cruel kind of justice.Sakaba isn't coming. No one is. We’re not worth saving.Let Alpha rest.";
	icon_state = "paper_neo_words_crumpled_bloodied"
	},
/turf/simulated/floor/industrial,
/area/iskhod/dungeon/outside/prepper/alpha)
